---
import { ArrowLeft } from "@lucide/astro";
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { profile } from "@data/profile";
import "@styles/account.css";
---
<BaseLayout active="utilities" title="Utility account privacy | Austin Garrod" description="How optional utility accounts use your email and saved progress." noIndex privatePage>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container page-hero-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Utility accounts</p><h1>Your account data.</h1>
    <p>Radius Map requires an account to save measurements. Pokémon Binder Tracker and Idle Slayer Companion support guest saves and file backups.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container account-layout assistant-layout rr-block" data-analytics-private>
    <div class="account-panel">
      <h2>What an account stores</h2>
      <p>Signing in creates an account with your verified email address. If you use Google, the site receives your email address and Google account identifier to recognize your sign-in. It requests no access to Gmail, Drive, contacts, or other Google content.</p>
      <p>Pokémon Binder Tracker syncs collected Pokémon, named set binders, card finishes, custom extras, and layout settings. Idle Slayer Companion syncs normalized progress, intentions, checkpoints, and saved comparison. Selected game-save files stay in your browser. Radius Map syncs saved names, location labels, exact centre coordinates, distances, and visibility.</p>
      <p>If you enable Binder stock alerts, the site saves your chosen stores and minimum card counts. Scheduled checks send card lookup details to Shopify and use your verified account email for notifications. You can turn off any store’s emails in Buy cards.</p>
      <h2>Where it is kept</h2>
      <p>Account records, secure sign-in sessions, synced utility documents, and recovery copies are stored with the site on HostPapa. Sign-in codes are sent through HostPapa email. Google processes its own sign-in flow when you choose that option. Utility data is not sent to Google for synchronization.</p>
      <p>Austin Garrod can review account details, synced saves, recovery copies, and stock-alert settings to respond to support requests and investigate sync issues. Access through the utility admin panel is recorded in a private access log.</p>
      <p>This is account-based synchronization, not end-to-end encrypted storage. Keep downloaded backups and migration recovery files private; they contain your saved data.</p>
      <h2>Recovery and deletion</h2>
      <p>Routine sync keeps checkpoints for up to three days with changes per save. Copies made for migrations, conflicts, restores, and other save replacements stay available until you delete them. Restoring a version preserves the version it replaces. Deleting one recovery copy does not delete the active save, other copies, browser originals, or hosting backups.</p>
      <p>For account access, export, or deletion requests, <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>contact Austin Garrod</a> using the email address associated with your account. Do not email sign-in codes, session cookies, or private sync keys.</p>
      <h2>Assistant connections</h2>
      <p>If you connect Codex or Claude, the service receives the catalog results and synced save details used in your conversation. You choose read or write access for each utility and can revoke it from Connected assistants. Save changes made through a connection use the same account recovery copies.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and diagnostics</h2>
      <p>A secure session cookie keeps you signed in across this site. Sign-out ends that session; sign-out everywhere ends all account sessions. Browser account copies and pending edits remain on their original device.</p>
      <p>Account and recovery pages do not load usage analytics or session recordings. Authentication and synchronization payloads are excluded from application diagnostics and recordings. Other site pages and utilities retain their existing analytics and privacy controls.</p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="/account/"><ArrowLeft size={16} aria-hidden="true" />Back to your account</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
